## Diagram 4 — Error-recovery state machine

Fault-confinement FSM driven by bus, socket, and SPI events.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> NORMAL

    NORMAL --> WARNING   : TEC/REC >= 96
    WARNING --> ERROR_PASSIVE : TEC/REC >= 127
    ERROR_PASSIVE --> BUS_OFF : TEC > 255

    BUS_OFF --> RECOVERING : 128 recessive bits<br/>ISO 11898-1 recovery
    RECOVERING --> NORMAL : Recovery complete
    BUS_OFF --> RESET : Manual reset / SPI fault
    RESET --> NORMAL : Reset complete
    NORMAL --> RESET : SPI fault / manual reset

    WARNING --> NORMAL : Counters decay < 96
    ERROR_PASSIVE --> WARNING : Counters < 127
    RECOVERING --> BUS_OFF : Recovery timeout
    RESET --> NORMAL : on_recovered callback

    state "Error Recovery" as ER {
        [*] --> IDLE
        IDLE --> WAITING : bus-off detected
        WAITING --> RESET_ISSUED : bus idle
        RESET_ISSUED --> RECOVERING : reset complete
        RECOVERING --> RECOVERED : 128 sequences elapsed
        RECOVERED --> [*]
        RESET_ISSUED --> FAILED : reset attempts exhausted
        WAITING --> FAILED : bus-idle timeout
    }

    note right of NORMAL
        Thresholds:
        WARNING 96 · PASSIVE 127 · BUS_OFF 256
    end note
```

