## How to render / validate

These diagrams use standard Mermaid syntax (`graph`, `flowchart`, `sequenceDiagram`,
`stateDiagram-v2`) and are compatible with:

- GitHub / GitLab Markdown rendering
- VS Code "Markdown: Preview Mermaid Diagrams" or the Mermaid Preview extension
- [Mermaid Live Editor](https://mermaid.live)
- [`mermaid-cli`](https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid-cli) (`mmdc`) for
  static PNG/SVG export:

```bash
# Install once
npm install -g mermaid-cli

# Export each diagram to SVG
mmdc -i docs/ARCHITECTURE.mmd -o architecture.svg
```

> `mmdc` extracts the first fenced Mermaid block per file. To export a
> specific diagram, place it in its own `.mmd` file or use the `--page` /
> sequence options supported by your `mermaid-cli` version.